waivers:
  - finding: "listen.rs:224 - with no state file (first launch or a lost file) the startup reconcile prints every existing non-router comment on every open task as a comment line (verified important)"
    reason: "deliberate, test-locked W3 behaviour: webhook_listen_registers_reconciles_then_prints_a_line_per_signed_transition starts with no state and asserts an existing owner comment prints before listening (W3 result: startup prints an unseen owner comment). Without state the listener cannot tell an acknowledged comment from an unacknowledged one and errs loud; a silent baseline would lose an owner comment posted while no listener ran, and a comment line is reply/acknowledge, never a lifecycle step, so a replay is noise, not a wrong action"
  - finding: "listen.rs:170-177, 227-230 - the seen map keeps answered, closed and done tasks (only a 404 prunes) and save_state rewrites the whole map per change, growing with lifetime task count (verified important)"
    reason: "each retained entry is that task's comment watermark: observe falls back to Seen::default(), so pruning a done task's entry makes the next delivery for it (an owner comment on a done task, an undone) replay its whole comment history. Growth is about 40 B per task of one single-owner project (epics, WUs, owner tasks), the reconcile walks open tasks only, and the rewrite is one small local file; bounding it needs a different watermark design, recorded as debt in the epic result"
nits:
